   "body": "OAI UPF (Simple Switch datapath) sends GTP-U Error Indication (message type 26)\nwith S=0 and an 8-octet header, however TS 29.281 clause 5.1 requires S=1 for Error\nIndication (optional header present, Sequence Number may be ignored by the peer).\nHeader TEID is correctly set to 0 and mandatory IEs are correct.\n\nA peer that validates the header may reject the message as malformed and never\nrun TS 23.527 \u00a75.3.3.1 recovery.\n\n# Details\n\nFrom TS 29.281 clause 5.1 (also reflected in UPF header comments in\n`gtpv1u/3gpp_29.281.hpp`):\n\n- For Error Indication, the **S flag shall be set to '1'**.\n- For Error Indication, **header TEID shall be all zeros** (failed TEID is only in\n  **TEID Data I**, Table 7.3.1-1 / clause 8.3).\n\n# Tests\n\nSetup: OAI RAN + OAI CN5G, Simple Switch UPF (`enable_bpf_datapath: no`).\nTrigger: restart `oai-upf`, then UE UL with stale N3 outgoing TEID.\n\nSee:\n\n[EI-OAICN5G.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/32094267/EI-OAICN5G.zip)\n\n```\n30 1a 00 0c 00 00 00 00          flags 0x30 (S=0), type 26, len 12, TEID 0\n10 00 00 00 1e                   TEID-I = 0x1e\n85 00 04 c0 a8 46 81             Peer Address = 192.168.70.129\n```\n\n# Possible cause\n\n`upf_n3::report_error_indication()` (simpleswitch/simple_switch.cpp) sets header TEID 0 and mandatory IEs, but never sets a sequence number.\n\n`gtpu_l4_stack::send_indication()` (gtpv1u/gtpv1u.cpp) only calls msg.set_sequence_number(sn) if get_sequence_number() is true. With no SN, encode keeps S=0.\n\n",
